$DATUM 3-epi-3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-methyl reserpate (12) Under N2 atmosphere, an
oven-dried 20 mL vial was charged with reserpine derivative S10 (100 mg,
0.241 mmol, 1.00 equiv), KF (28.0 mg, 0.482 mmol, 2.00 equiv) and
PhenoFluor (154 mg, 0.362 mmol, 1.50 equiv). Toluene (5.0 mL) was added,
followed by N,N-diisopropylethylamine (62.4 mg, 84.0 μL, 0.483 mmol, 2.00
equiv). The reaction mixture was stirred in a sealed vial and heated at
80 °C for 16 h. Once cooled to 23 °C, the reaction mixture was
concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by chromatography on
silica gel, eluting with CH2Cl2/MeOH 20:1 (v/v)→15:1 (v/v), to afford
82.4 mg of the title compound. 3-epi-3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-methyl reserpate
(12), colorless solid (82% yield) NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 7.23 (d, J = 7.8, 1H), 6.87 (d, J = 1.0 Hz, 1H), 6.69
(dd, J = 8.0, 2.1 Hz, 1H), 5.09 (d, JCF = 51.3 Hz, 1H), 4.22 (br. s.,
1H), 3.83 (s, 3H), 3.81 (s, 3H), 3.60 (ddd, J = 28.4, 11.4, 1.0 Hz, 1H),
3.47 (s, 3H), 3.02 (dd, J = 11.4, 5.0 Hz, 1H), 2.84 (dd, J = 11.2, 5.3
Hz, 1H), 2.67–2.60 (m, 2H), 2.30–2.05 (m, 5H), 1.97–1.80 (m, 4H). 13C NMR
(125 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 173.2, 161.2, 154.2, 132.7, 122.5, 118.8,
111.6, 107.0, 95.4, 87.3 (d, JCF = 188.6), 81.0, 76.0 (d, JCF = 18.3 Hz),
57.4, 55.6, 54.2, 52.1, 49.1, 47.4, 36.7, 31.1, 30.0, 29.3 (d, JCF = 22.9
Hz), 21.8. 19F NMR (375 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 197.1. Mass Spectrometry:
HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z): Calcd for [C23H29FN2O4 + H]+, 417.2184. Found,
417.2181.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Late-Stage Deoxyfluorination of Alcohols with PhenoFluor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
