$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-Fluoroisoquinoline (17) A mixture of 5-hydroxyisoquinoline (80.6 mg,
0.500 mmol) and PhenoFluorMix (1.10 g) in toluene (5.0 mL) was stirred at
23°C for 30 min, then at 110°C for 24 hours. Purification by flash silica
gel column chromatography (EtOAc in hexanes = 5%-15%). 59.9 mg of the
title compound as a yellow oil (81% yield). R f = 0.22 (EtOAc in hexanes
= 20%). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3, 23°C, δ): 9.28 (s, 1H),
8.59 (d, J = 5.9 Hz, 1H), 7.87 (d, J = 5.4 Hz, 1H), 7.77 (d, J = 7.8 Hz,
1H), 7.53 (td, J = 7.8, 5.4 Hz, 1H), 7.35 (dd, J = 9.8, 7.8 Hz, 1H). 13C
NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 23°C, δ): 157.6 (d, J = 253.7 Hz), 152.1 (d, J = 2.9
Hz), 143.5, 129.7 (d, J = 4.8 Hz), 127.3 (d, J = 6.7 Hz), 126.5 (d, J =
17.2 Hz), 123.5 (d, J = 4.8 Hz), 114.0 (d, J = 19.1 Hz), 113.5 (d, J =
2.9 Hz). 19F NMR (470 MHz, CDCl3, 23°C, δ): -126.2. HRMS-FIA(m/z) calc’d
for C9H7FN [M+H]+, 148.0557; found, 148.0562.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM PhenoFluorMix: Practical Chemoselective Deoxyfluorination of Phenols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fujimoto, Teppei; Ritter, Tobias
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(3), 544-547

