$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 6-epi-6-Fluoro-6-deoxy-3-O-Bz-morphine (9) For the synthesis of S9, see
section “Synthesis and characterization of non-commercially available
starting materials". Under N2 atmosphere, an oven-dried 20 mL vial was
charged with 3-O-Bz-morphine S9 (100 mg, 0.257 mmol, 1.00 equiv), KF
(29.9 mg, 0.514 mmol, 2.00 equiv), and PhenoFluor (163 mg, 0.385 mmol,
1.50 equiv). Dichloromethane (4.0 mL) was added, followed by
N,N-diisopropylethylamine (89 μL, 0.51 mmol, 2.0 equiv). The reaction
mixture was stirred in a sealed vial at 23 °C for 16 h. The reaction
mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel, eluting with Et2O/MeOH 30:1 (v/v), to
afford 81.0 mg of the title compound.
6-epi-6-Fluoro-6-deoxy-3-O-Bz-morphine (9), colorless oil (80% yield) Rf
= 0.25 (Et2O/MeOH 30:1 (v/v)). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3,
23 °C, δ): 8.21–8.19 (m, 2H), 7.63 (t, 1H, J = 7.4 Hz), 7.50 (t, 2H, J =
7.7 Hz), 6.90 (d, 1H, J = 8.2 Hz), 6.67 (d, 1H, J = 8.2 Hz), 6.00–5.97
(m, 1H), 5.85 (dd, 1H, J = 9.3 Hz, J = 7.0 Hz), 4.99–4.89 (m, 2H),
3.39–3.37 (m, 1H), 3.13–3.06 (m, 2H), 2.61 (dd, 1H, J = 12.2 Hz, J = 4.6
Hz), 2.45 (s, 3H), 2.40–2.34 (m, 2H), 2.12 (dt, 1H, J = 12.4 Hz, J = 5.0
Hz), 1.91 (d, 1H, J = 12.5 Hz). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ):
164.4, 148.7, 137.7 (d, JCF = 10.1 Hz), 133.8, 132.9, 132.1, 131.3,
130.5, 130.5, 129.4, 128.8, 128.8, 126.8 (d, JCF = 14.1 Hz), 122.2,
