$DATUM Methyl 3b-Acetoxy-30-fluorolup-20(29)-en-28-oate (6b) To a stirred
solution of alcohol 6a (100 mg, 0.18 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL), cooled to
-78 °C was added DAST (100 mL, 0.52 mmol). The reaction mixture was then
allowed to warm to r.t. and then quenched by addition of H2O (1 mL). The
separated organic layer was diluted with CHCl3 (50 mL), washed with H2O
(2 × 40 mL), dried (MgSO4) and evaporated under reduced pressure. The
residue was separated by HPLC (6% EtOAc in hexane) and crystallized from
MeOH to give 6b. Dark yellow residue, yield 80 mg, 80%. mp 219-221 °C; [α
]D25 -6.0 (c = 0.37). IR (CHCl3): 1256 (C-O-C), 1655 (C=C), 1721 cm-1
(C=O). 1H NMR: δ = 0.83 (s, 3 H), 0.84 (s, 3 H), 0.84 (s, 3 H), 0.91 (s,
3 H), 0.96 (s, 3 H), 2.04 (s, 3 H), 2.95 (td, 1 H, J= 11.1, 4.4 Hz, H-19β
), 3.67 (s, 3 H, CO2CH3), 4.47 (m, 1 H, S J= 16.0 Hz, H-3a), 4.84 (d, 2
H, J= 47.5 Hz, H-30), 5.02 (m, 2 H, S J= 6.3 Hz, H-29). 13C NMR: δ = 38.4
(C-1), 23.7 (C-2), 80.9 (C-3), 37.8 (C-4), 55.4 (C-5), 18.2 (C-6), 34.2
(C-7), 40.7 (C-8), 50.4 (C-9), 37.1 (C-10), 21.0 (C-11), 26.7 (C-12),
38.2 (C-13), 42.3 (C-14), 29.7 (C-15), 32.0 (C-16), 56.6 (C-17), 50.1
(C-18), 42.2 (C-19), 150.1 (d, J = 12.2 Hz, C-20), 27.3 (C-21), 36.6
(C-22), 27.9 (C-23), 16.5 (C- 24), 16.2 (C-25), 15.9 (C-26), 14.6 (C-27),
176.5 (C-28), 110.9 (d, J = 11.1 Hz, C-29), 85.0 (d, J = 169 Hz, C-30),
21.3 (3b-OCOCH3), 171.0 (3b-OCOCH3), 51.3 (CO2CH3). 19F NMR: δ = -215.22
(td, J= 47.3, 2.3 Hz). MS: m/z (%) = 530 (M+, 63), 510 (20), 470 (100),
455 (42), 427 (14), 411 (14), 291 (13), 219 (13), 207 (19), 189 (56).
Anal. Calcd for C33H51FO4: C, 74.68; H, 9.69; F, 3.58. Found: C, 74.34;
H, 9.72; F, 3.66.
