$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):RGT(2):CAS_RN
$DATUM 603-35-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
(rel)-(1S,2R)-(3-Bromomethyl-2,2-difluoro-1-methyl-cyclopropylmethoxy)-t-butyldimethylsilane
(14) The alcohol 12 (415 mg, 1.56 mmol) was dissolved in CH2Cl2 (10 mL)
and triphenylphosphine (846 mg, 3.12 mmol) was added, which was followed
by the slow addition of N-bromosuccinimide (559 mg, 3.12 mmol) at 0°C .
After the addition was complete, the solution was stirred for 5 hours at
room temperature and diluted with CH2Cl2 (50 mL). The organic phase was
washed with water (50 mL) and brine, dried over anhydrous magnesium
sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. The crude product was purified by
quick flash column chromatography (EtOAc/hexane, 1:15).
(rel)-(1R,2R)-(3-Bromomethyl-2,2-difluoro-1-methyl-cyclopropylmethoxy)-t-butyldimethylsilane
(15) Bromide derivative 15 was synthesized from 13 by a similar procedure
as described for 14: yield 80%. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300 MHz) δ 3.79-3.70 (m,
2H), 3.26-3.19 (m, 2H), 1.61-1.54 (m, 1H), 1.18 (s, 3H), 0.83 (s, 9H),
0.01 (s, 6H).
