$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 2: DAST (83 g, 0.51 mol) was added dropwise to a stirred solution of
1-[4- (benzyloxy)phenyl]-1-(6-bromopyridin-3-yl)-2,2-dimethylpropan-1-ol
(80 g, 0.19 mol) in CH2Cl2 (1 L) and CHCl3 (120 mL) at 0 °C. The
resulting mixture was stirred at rt for 4 h, then quenched by the
addition of water. The combined organic layer was washed with saturated
NaHCO3 (aq) and brine, dried, filtered and concentrated. The residue was
recrystallised from EtOH. Compound 2 as a solid (65 g, 80%). 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.60 (d, J = 2.5 Hz, 1H), 7.68 (dd, J = 2.6, 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.30 – 7.47 (m, 8H), 6.94 (d, J = 8.9 Hz, 2H), 5.05 (s, 2H), 1.13 (s,
9H); MS m/z 430.0 (M+H)+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of AZD6642, an Inhibitor of 5-Lipoxygenase Activating Protein
(FLAP) for the Treatment of Inflammatory Diseases
