$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-Fmoc-serine methyl ester (2)
Under N2 atmosphere, an oven-dried 20 mL vial was charged with
Fmoc-serine-methyl ester (100 mg, 0.293 mmol, 1.00 equiv) and PhenoFluor
(150 mg, 0.352 mmol, 1.50 equiv). Dioxane (6.0 mL) was added. The
reaction mixture was stirred in a sealed vial at 23 °C for 3 h. The
reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel, eluting with pentane/Et2O 3:2 (v/v), to
afford 70.0 mg of the title compound as a colorless solid (71% yield).
3-Fluoro-3-deoxy-Fmoc-serine methyl ester (2), yield (80%) Rf = 0.40
(pentane/Et2O 3:2 (v/v)). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR (600 MHz, CDCl3, 23
°C, δ): 7.78 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 2H), 7.61 (t, J = 6.7 Hz, 2H), 7.41 (t, J =
7.3 Hz, 2H), 7.33 (t, J = 7.9 Hz, 2H), 5.67 (d, J = 7.6 Hz, 1H), 4.85
(ddd, J = 46.0, 9.4, 2.1, 1H), 4.69 (ddd, J = 47.4, 9.4, 2.1, 1H), 4.59
(dd, J = 33.1, 8.5 Hz, 1H), 4.43 (m, 2H), 4.25 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 3.84
(s, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): 169.4, 155.9, 143.8, 143.7,
141.4, 141.4, 127.8, 127.8, 127.2, 127.2, 125.2, 125.2, 120.1, 120.1,
83.3 (d, JCF = 173.5 Hz), 67.5, 54.8 (d, JCF = 19.7 Hz), 53.1, 47.1. 19F
NMR (375 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): -232.0. Mass Spectrometry: HRMS (ESI-TOF)
(m/z): Calcd for [C19H18FNO4 + H]+, 344.1293. Found, 344.1299.
