$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General procedure for volatile compound An oven-dried vial was charged
with PhenoFluorMix (220 mg, corresponding to 1.50 equiv of the
chloroimidazolium chloride to a substrate). PhenoFluorMix was heated at
140°C for 1 hour under vacuum (~0.1 Torr). After the mixture was cooled
to 23°C, a phenol or a heterocycle (0.100 mmol, 1.00 equiv) was quickly
added. The vial was evacuated and backfilled with N2 gas, then toluene or
xylene (1.0 mL) was added via syringe. The mixture was stirred at 23°C
for 30 min and subsequently heated at 110°C or 140°C for 24 hours. The
reaction mixture was cooled to 23°C, then 1-fluoro-3-nitrobenzene (10.0
μL, 0.0939 mmol, 0.939 equiv) was added to the mixture. The yields were
determined by comparing the integration of the 19F NMR (470 MHz, 23°C,
toluene or xylene) resonance of the fluorinated product with that of
1-fluoro-3-nitrobenzene (-112.0 ppm). Product:
4-fluoro-1,2-dimethoxybenzene (8). Yield: 79%. 19F NMR (ppm): -123.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM volatile product; 19F-NMR yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM PhenoFluorMix: Practical Chemoselective Deoxyfluorination of Phenols
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Fujimoto, Teppei; Ritter, Tobias
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(3), 544-547

