$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 10β-Fluoro-10-deoxy-dihydroartemisinin (8) Under N2 atmosphere, an
oven-dried vial was charged with dihydroartemisinin (25.0 mg, 0.0880
mmol, 1.00 equiv), KF (10.2 mg, 0.176 mmol, 2.00 equiv) and PhenoFluor
(56.0 mg, 0.132 mmol, 1.50 equiv). Toluene (1.3 mL) was added, followed
by N,N-diisopropylethylamine (31 μL, 0.18 mmol, 2.0 equiv). The reaction
mixture was stirred in a sealed vial and heated at 80 °C for 12 h. Once
cooled to 23 °C, the reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The
resultant solid mixture was triturated with pentane and the solids were
separated. The solids were further triturated with pentane/Et2O 9:1 (v/v)
and finally discarded. The liquid phases were combined and concentrated
under reduced pressure to obtain a crude mixture that contained the
desired product and a variable amount of urea derived from PhenoFluor.
The mixture was quickly purified by flash column chromatography on silica
gel eluting with pentane/Et2O 9:1 (v/v) to afford 20.0 mg of the title
compound as a clorless crystalline solid (79%). NOTE: the product was
found to be prone to decomposition under acidic conditions and in
chloroform solution. A fast purification on silica is essential to obtain
a pure product. Alternatively, the product has been been purified using
Florosil.13. 10β-Fluoro-10-deoxy-dihydroartemisinin (8), clorless
crystalline solid (79%) Rf = 0.45 (pentane/Et2O 9:1 (v/v)). 1H NMR (500
MHz, C6D6, 23 °C, δ): 5.53 (s, 1H), 5.51 (d, JHF = 55.2 Hz, 1H), 2.55
(dm, JHF = 35.6 Hz, 1H), 2.26 (dt, J = 3.9, 13.9 Hz, 1H), 1.72–1.62 (m,
1H), 1.58–1.35 (m, 3H), 1.32 (s, 3H), 1.29–1.15 (m, 3H), 0.98 (dt, J =
6.8, 11.2 Hz, 1H), 0.81 - 0.69 (m, 1H), 0.63 (s, 6H), 0.59–0.46 (m, 1H).
13C NMR (125 MHz, C6D6, 23 °C, δ):110.9 (d, JCF = 221.3 Hz), 104.2, 88.7,
52.2, 43.7 (d, JCF = 2.6 Hz), 37.0, 36.4, 34.5, 30.9, 30.8 (d, JCF = 22.2
Hz),, 25.8, 24.9, 24.2, 20.1, 12.1 (d, JCF = 1.7 Hz). 19F NMR (375 MHz,
C6D6, 23 °C, δ): –134.0. Mass Spectrometry: HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z): Calcd
for [C15H23FO4 + H]+, 287.1653. Found, 287.1657.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Late-Stage Deoxyfluorination of Alcohols with PhenoFluor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
