$DATUM rac-3-(3-Fluoropyrrolidine-1-carbonyl)-benzaldehyde (6) For the synthesis
of S8, see section “Synthesis and characterization of non-commercially
available starting materials". Under N2 atmosphere, an oven-dried 20 mL
vial was charged with S8 (100 mg, 0.456 mmol, 1.00 equiv), KF (53.0 mg,
0.912 mmol, 2.00 equiv), and PhenoFluor (290 mg, 0.684 mmol, 1.50 equiv).
Toluene (7.0 mL) was added, followed by N,N-diisopropylethylamine (117.9
mg, 159 μL, 0.912 mmol, 2.00 equiv). The reaction mixture was stirred in
a sealed vial and heated at 80 °C for 12 h. Once cooled to 23 °C, the
reaction mixture was concentrated in vacuo. The residue was purified by
chromatography on silica gel, eluting with pentane/EtOAc 1:3 (v/v), to
afford 78.0 mg of the title compound.
rac-3-(3-Fluoropyrrolidine-1-carbonyl)-benzaldehyde (6), colorless oil
(77% yield) Rf = 0.35 (pentane/EtOAc 1:3 (v/v)). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR
(600 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, ): [mixture of 2 rotamers] 10.03 (br. s., 1H,
major + minor), 8.05 (s, 1H, major), 8.00 (s, 1H, minor), 7.97–7.93 (m,
1H, major + minor), 7.81 (d, J = 7.3 Hz, 1H, major), 7.78 (d, J = 7.3 Hz,
1H, minor), 7.62–7.57 (m, 1H, major + minor), 5.33 (d, J = 52.1 Hz, 1H,
major), 5.21 (d, J = 52.1 Hz, 1H, minor), 4.00–3.51 (m, 4H, major +
minor), 2.41–1.93 (m, 2H, major + minor). 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C,
δ): [mixture of 2 rotamers] 191.5, 168.7, 168.5, 137.6, 137.5, 136.5,
133.2, 133.1, 131.3, 131.3, 129.5, 129.4, 128.5, 128.2, 93.2, 92.3, 91.8,
90.9, 55.8, 55.6, 53.3, 53.1, 47.1, 44.3, 33.4, 33.2, 31.3, 31.1. 19F NMR
(375 MHz, CDCl3, 23 °C, δ): [mixture of 2 rotamers] 173.0 (major), 173.8
(minor). Mass Spectrometry: HRMS (ESI-TOF) (m/z): Mass Spectrometry: HRMS
(ESI-TOF) (m/z): Calcd for [C12H12FNO2 + H]+, 222.0925. Found, 220.0928.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used, sealed vial used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Late-Stage Deoxyfluorination of Alcohols with PhenoFluor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
