$DATUM Fluoro Ketone 5b To a stirred solution of enol ketone 5a (107 mg, 0.23
mmol) in CH2Cl2 (5 mL), cooled to -78 °C was added DAST (100 mL, 0.52
mmol). The reaction mixture was then allowed to warm to r.t. and then
quenched by addition of H2O (1 mL). The separated organic layer was
diluted with CHCl3 (50 mL), washed with H2O (2 × 40 mL), dried (MgSO4)
and evaporated under reduced pressure. The dark yellow residue was
separated by HPLC (6% EtOAc in hexane) to give fluoro ketone 5b. White
crystalline solid, yield 81 mg, 77%. mp 231-233 °C (MeOH); [α ]D25 +75 (c
= 0.17). IR (CHCl3): 1616 (C=C), 1689 cm-1 (C=O). 1H NMR: δ = 0.81 (s, 3
H), 0.84 (d, 3 H, J = 0.9 Hz), 0.94 (d, 3 H, J= 0.9 Hz), 0.94 (s, 3 H),
1.02 (s, 3 H), 1.09 (s, 3 H), 1.10 (s, 3 H), 2.86 (dt, 1 H, J= 16.1, 2.1
Hz, H-1), 3.46 (d, 1 H, J= 7.9 Hz, H- 28α ), 3.55 (s, 1 H, H-19α ), 3.79
(dd, 1 H, J= 7.8, 1.4 Hz, H-28β ), 7.35 (ddd, 1 H, J= 82.6, 3.1, 1.5 Hz,
H-31). 13C NMR: δ = 38.5 (C-1), 119.7 (C-2), 207.0 (C-3), 45.5 (C-4),
53.1 (C-5), 20.1 (C-6), 32.7 (C-7), 40.4 (C-8), 48.9 (C-9), 35.8 (C-10),
21.7 (C-11), 26.4 (C-12), 34.3 (C-13), 40.8 (C-14), 26.4 (C-15), 36.7
(C-16), 41.5 (C-17), 46.8 (C-18), 87.9 (C-19), 36.3 (C-20), 32.8 (C-21),
26.2 (C-22), 28.8 (C-23), 22.0 (C-24), 15.3 (C-25), 16.0 (C-26), 13.4
(C-27), 71.3 (C-28), 24.5 (C-29), 28.7 (C-30), 156.8 (d, J = 278 Hz,
C-31). 19F NMR: δ = -121.14 (ddd, J= 82.4, 6.4 Hz, 4.1 Hz). MS: m/z (%) =
470 (M+, 100), 450 (15), 439 (23), 399 (69), 383 (1), 341 (1), 323 (1),
215 (14), 203 (6), 189 (7). Anal. Calcd for C31H47FO2: C, 79.10; H,
10.06; F, 4.04. Found: C, 79.34; H, 9.76; F, 4.53.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety (- DAST can decompose explosively above 55 C)
