$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):PRO(1):YIELD
$DATUM 76
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: To a reactor with a TeflonTM PFA tube with a
diameter of 10 mm sealed at one end, 1a (137 mg, 1 mmol) and DFBA (478
mg, 2.4 mmol) were introduced. The open end of the reactor was connected
to a reflux condenser. Then, the reactor part was submitted to
microwave-irradiation (IDX microwave oven for organic synthesis
IMCR-25003) for 10 min and during the irradiation the temperature was
kept at 70 °C. After cooling, the reaction mixture was poured into an aq
solution of NaHCO3. The product was extracted with Et2O (3 ×) and the
combined ethereal layers were dried over MgSO4. Purification by column
chromatography (silica gel, hexane-Et2O) gave 2a. 2c, yield 76%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, microwave irradiation, IDX microwave oven used, no
solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (fluoroalkyl)amines by deoxyfluorination of amino alcohols
