$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of α -Chlorobenzylphosphonates from
α -Hydroxyphosphonates. A solution of 1k (1.00 g, 3.46 mmol, 1.0 equiv)
and Ph3P (1.36 g, 5.19 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in dry CCl4 (10 mL) is refluxed
for 8 h under argon. Then, the mixture is evaporated under reduced
pressure, and the semisolid residue is extracted with PE. The combined
extracts are filtered, and the solvent is removed under reduced pressure.
The crude material was purified by flash column chromatography on silica
gel to yield 3k. Diethyl α -chloro-4-nitrobenzylphosphonate (3k). Yellow
oil, yield (0.81 g, 76%). 1HNMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.26 (t, J = 7.0
Hz, 3H), 1.35 (t, J = 7.0 Hz, 3H), 4.00-4.14 (m, 2H), 4.15-4.28 (m, 2H),
5.00 (d, 2JPH = 15.2 Hz, 1H), 7.73 (d, J = 8.6 Hz, 2H), 8.25 (d, J = 8.6
Hz, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 16.2 (d, 3JPC = 5.6 Hz), 16.4
(d, 3JPC = 5.7 Hz), 52.5 (d, 1JPC = 156.4 Hz), 64.1 (d, 2JPC = 7.0 Hz),
64.6 (d, 2JPC = 7.0 Hz), 123.6, 129.8, 141.4, 148.0 ppm; HRMS (EI) [M+H]+
308.0450, Calculated Mass 308.0455.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The first synthesis of diethyl α,α-chlorofluorobenzylphosphonates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wu, Di; He, Yanhong; Tang, Rongchang; Guan, Zhi
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2009), (13), 2180-2182

