$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Halogenation Conditions for Compounds 17-19. Into a 100 mL
round-bottom flask were added the allylic alcohol (5.05 mmol),
N,N-diisopropylethylamine (1.41 mL, 8.09 mmol), and 30 mL of dry
acetonitrile. The solution was stirred at 0 °C for 10 min. Solid
dichlorotriphenylphosphorane (2.45 g, 7.58 mmol) was then added evenly to
the reaction mixture over a 7 min period. After the final addition of
Ph3PCl2, the reaction was allowed to stir at 0 °C for an additional 40
min. The mixture was then loaded directly onto a silica gel column and
purified by flash chromatography (5% EtOAc in hexane).
8-(p-Nitroaniline)-3,7-dimethyl-1-chloro-2,6-octadiene (17). 1.17 g (75%)
of a bright lemon yellow oil. TLC: (Rf 0.56).
