$DATUM tert-Butyl cis
-5-[5-[(1S,2R)-2-(2-fluoroethyl)cyclopropyl]pyridin-3-yl]hexahydropyrrolo[3,4-c]pyrrole-2(1H)-carboxylate
(14). To a stirred solution of 12 (0.393 g, 1.05 mmol) in anhydrous
CH2Cl2 (5 mL) was added DMAP (25 mg, 0.21 mmol), Et3N (0.43 mL, 3.15
mmol), and p-TsCl (0.30 g, 1.58 mmol) at 0 °C. The reaction was allowed
to warm to rt and stirred overnight, then CH2Cl2 (25 mL) was added, and
the mixture was washed successively with aqueous NaHCO3, water, and
brine. After drying the extracts over Na2SO4 and concentrating under
reduced pressure, the crude product followed by purified by column
chromatography (silica gel) using hexane/EtOAc (3:1). The tosylate
obtained was not stable and was used immediately in the next reaction. A
1.0 M solution of tetra-n-butylammonium fluoride in THF (3 mL) was added
to the p-toluenesulfonate (0.12 g, 0.023 mmol), and the resulting
solution was stirred overnight and then concentrated under reduced
pressure and purified by column chromatrography using 50‒60% EtOAc in
hexane as the eluent to yield 14. Colorless oil, yield 0.12 g (74%). 1H
NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 7.76 (s, 2H), 6.42 (s, 1H), 4.60 (t, J = 6 Hz,
1H), 4.48 (t, J = 6 Hz, 1H), 3.62 (s, 2H), 3.51 (s, 2H), 3.35-3.19 (m,
4H), 2.99 (s, 2H), 1.86‒1.72 (m, 2H), 1.67‒1.63 (m, 1H), 1.44 (s, 9H),
1.16‒1.13 (m, 1H), 0.97‒0.93 (m, 1H), 0.87‒0.83 (m, 1H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
100 MHz) δ 154.6, 143.5, 138.9, 136.1, 132.0, 115.5, 84.6 (d, JC-F =
164.6 Hz), 79.7, 51.9, 50.5, 50.2, 42.2, 41.3, 35.1 (d, JC-F = 19.5 Hz),
28.6, 20.6, 19.3 (d, JC-F = 6.9 Hz), 15.2.
