$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure B: One-Pot, Two-Step
Conversion of Aryl Alcohols to Aryl Fluorides. Nonaflation Step. Aryl
alcohol (1.0 mmol) and perfluoro-1-butanesulfonyl fluoride (453 mg, 1.5
mmol) dissolved in 2 mL of dry toluene was added by syringe to a capped
vial with CsF (320 mg, 2.0 mmol). (For aryl alcohols poorly soluble in
toluene, the reaction vial was quickly uncapped and the alcohol added as
dry material before recapping and flushing with N2.) The reaction was
stirred at 50 °C for the times indicated in Table 2. Fluorination Step.
Tris(dibenzylideneacetone)dipalladium(0) (18 mg, 0.020 mmol) and
t-BuBrettPhos (29 mg, 0.060 mmol) (Pd:L = 1:1.5) in 2 mL of dry toluene
was stirred in a dried glass vial for about 5 min at room temperature.
The mixture was then added by syringe to the previous reaction mixture
through the septum and the resulting reaction mixture was microwave
heated at 180 °C for 30 minutes. After being cooled to room temperature,
the reaction mixture was purified by silica flash chromatography and
isolated using the conditions indicated below.
4-(3-Fluorophenyl)morpholine (2e).37 Synthesized from 3b according to
general procedure B. The reaction mixture was purified using 25-50%
dichloromethane in pentane as eluent to give 2e
4-Fluoro-7-methoxy-2-phenylquinoline (2k). Synthesized from 3k according
to general procedure B, using 1,4-dioxane/toluene 1:1 as solvent. The
reaction mixture was purified using 0-10% ethyl acetate in isohexane as
eluent to give 2k White solid; 186 mg, 73% yield. mp 87-89 °C. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 8.12-8.08 (m, 2H), 7.95 (dd, J = 8.0, 0.8 Hz 1H),
7.56-7.40 (m, 5H), 7.21 (dd, J = 9.1, 2.5 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (100.5 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 166.2 (d, JCF = 265 Hz), 161.9, 159.7 (d, JCF = 8 Hz), 152.5
(d, JCF = 5 Hz), 139.2 (d, JCF = 4 Hz), 129.8, 129.0, 127.5, 121.6 (d,
JCF = 5 Hz), 119.9 (d, JCF = 2 Hz), 113.3 (d, JCF = 13 Hz), 107.6 (d, JCF
= 4 Hz), 101.8 (d, JCF = 17 Hz), 55.7. 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3) δ:
-113.1. HRMS (ESI): calcd for C16H13FNO (M + H)+ 254.0981, found:
254.0986.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (stage 3), thermal (stage 3), capped vial used,
reaction mixture from stage 2 added to product from stage 1 in stage 3,
pre-dried CsF used, key intermediate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM One-Pot, Two-Step, Microwave-Assisted Palladium-Catalyzed Conversion of
Aryl Alcohols to Aryl Fluorides via Aryl Nonaflates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wannberg, Johan; Wallinder, Charlotta; Unlusoy, Meltem; Skoeld,
Christian; Larhed, Mats
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2013), 78(8), 4184-4189

