$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Into a stirred solution of 1.50 g (6.0 mmol) of 1k in 20 mL of dry
dichloromethane in a fluoropolymer vessel, 1.22 g (12.1 mmol) of
triethylamine was added at room temperature, followed by the addition of
a solution of 0.52 g (6.0 mmol) of (±)-3-pyrrolidinol (21) in 5 mL of dry
dichloromethane. The reaction mixture was refluxed for 10 h. After
cooling to room temperature, the reaction mixture was poured into an aq.
sodium carbonate solution. The mixture was extracted with
dichloromethane, and the organic layer was separated and dried on
anhydrous magnesium sulfate. After filtration, the filtrate was
evaporated to dryness and the residue was chromatographed on silica gel
using a 2:1 mixture of ether and hexane to give
1-(4'-tert-butyl-2',6'-dimethylphenylsulfinyl)-3-fluoropyrrolidine (22)
as a solid. Yield: 1.28 g (72%). 19F NMR showed that the product was a
1:0.66 mixture of two diastereoisomers.
1-(4'-tert-butyl-2',6'-dimethylphenylsulfinyl)-3-fluoropyrrolidine (22),
yield 1.28 g (72%). 19F-NMR (CDCl3) δ - 173.28 (m, 0.6F), -174.44 (m,
0.4F); 1H-NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.97 (s, 2H), 5.05-5.35 (m, 1H) 3.05-3.75 (m,
4H), 2.51 (s, 6H), 1.90-2.25 (m, 2H), 1.28 (s, 9H); 13C-NMR (CDCl3) a
major isomer: δ 153.3, 137.4, 134.6, 127.5, 93.0 (d, J = 178.4 Hz), 53.4,
(d, J = 23.8 Hz), 44.0, 34.5, 33.1 (d, J = 21.7 Hz), 31.2, 20.0; a minor
isomer: δ 153.3, 137.3, 134.9, 127.5, 19.98, 93.5 (d, J = 177.7 Hz), 51.6
(d, J = 23.8 Hz), 46.2, 34.5, 33.5 (d, J = 21.7 Hz), 31.2, 20.0. Anal
Calcd for C16H24FNOS: C, 64.61%; H, 8.13%; N, 4.71%. Found: C, 64.19%; H,
7.86%; N, 4.61%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, 1:0.66 stereoisomers, alternative reaction conditions
gave higher yield but no stereoselectivity, fluoropolymer vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
