$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7-O-(tert-Butyldiphenylsilyl)-4-deoxy-4-iodo-hept-2-ulopyranosonate 5
Alcohol 3a (70 mg, 0.15 mmol) was dissolved in anhyd toluene (8 mL) at
r.t. Imidazole (40.8 mg, 60 mmol, 4 equiv) and Ph3P (157 mg, 60 mmol, 4
equiv) were added. After I2 (171 mg, 67 mmol, 4.4 equiv) addition, the
soln was refluxed during 15 h. The mixture was then allowed to cool to
r.t. and diluted with EtOAc (20 mL). The organic phase was washed with
sat. aq NaHSO3 (8 × 6 mL), dried (MgSO4), and filtered and the solvents
were evaporated under reduced pressure. Filtration of the residue (silica
gel, Et2O-PE, 1:1) afforded pure 5. Yield 61 mg, 70%. Rf = 0.75 (Et2O-PE,
1:1). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.05 (s, 9 H, t-Bu), 1.32 (t, J = 7.1
Hz, 3 H, CH2CH3), 2.42 (dd, J = 14.1, 3.0 Hz, 1 H, H3), 2.87 (dd, J =
14.1, 7.7 Hz, 1 H, H3), 3.53 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 2 H, H7), 3.81 (t, J = 6.8
Hz, 1 H, H6), 4.11 (dd, J = 7.7, 3.1 Hz, 1 H, H4), 4.30 (q, J = 7.1 Hz, 2
H, CH2CH3), 4.93 (s, 1 H, H5), 7.3-7.5 (m, 6 H, HAr), 7.5-7.8 (m, 4 H,
HAr). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 14.0 (CH2CH3), 14.9 (C4), 19.2 (Cq
t-Bu), 26.8 (CH3 t-Bu), 49.5 (C3), 62.5 (CH2CH3), 63.5 (C7), 80.5 (C6),
86.2 (C5), 105.2 (C2), 127.8, 127.9, 129.9, 135.5 (CHAr), 132.9, 133.1
(Cq Ar), 164.5 (C1). HRMS: m/z [M+ + Na] calcd for C25H31INaO5Si:
589.0883; found: 589.0911.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
