$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-(2'-Fluoroethyl)-N-methyl-4-tert-butyl-2,6-dimethylbenzensulfinamide
(20) Step1: A solution of 0.60 g (8.0 mmol) of 2-(N-methylamino)ethanol
and 4 mmol of Et3N(HF)3 in 3 mL of dry 1,2-dichloroethane was added into
a stirred solution of 2.00 g (8.0 mmol) of 1k in 5 mL of dry
1,2-dichloroethane in a fluoropolymer vessel heated at 75 °C. After
complete addition, the mixture was stirred at 75 °C for 5 minutes and
then allowed to cool to room temperature slowly in 0.5 h. Step 2: Into
the reaction mixture of step 1, 2.93 g (29 mmol ) of triethylamine was
added slowly under stirring at room temperature. After 1 h stirring at
room temperature, 19F NMR analysis using a standard (fluorobenzene)
showed that the yield of product was 70%. To isolate the product, the
reaction mixture was poured into 1N NaOH solution and extracted with
dichloromethane. The organic layer was dried over anhydrous magnesium
sulfate and filtered. Removal of solvent at reduced pressure gave viscous
oil, which was then chromatographed on silica gel using ether:hexane
(2:1) as an eluent to give N-(2'-
fluoroethyl)-N-methyl-4-tert-butyl-2,6-dimethylbenzenesulfinamide (20).
Yeild: 1.38 g (65%).
N-(2'-Fluoroethyl)-N-methyl-4-tert-butyl-2,6-dimethylbenzensulfinamide
(20), yield 70%. M.p. 82-83 °C; 19F NMR (CDCl3) δ -219.82 (tt, 1F, J =
47.6, 27.2 Hz); 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.98 (s, 2H), 4.50 (dm, J = 47.1 Hz,
1H), 3.25-3.60 (m, 2H), 2.74 (s, 3H), 2.47 (s, 6H), 1.25 (s, 9H); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) δ 153.6, 137.9, 134.4, 127.6, 82.2 (d, J = 171.2 Hz), 52.9 (d, J
= 20.9 Hz), 34.5, 34.3, 31.2, 20.1; IR (neat) 2964, 1593, 1463, 1362,
1296, 1226, 1202, 1096, 1032, 875, 634 cm-1. HRMS (ESI/APCI method) Calcd
for C15H24FNNaOS (M + Na)+: 308.1455. Found: 308.1463. Anal Calcd for
C15H24FNOS: C, 63.12; H, 8.48; N, 4.91. Found: C, 63.03; H, 8.41; N,
4.87.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative reaction conditions with HF-py gave slightly lower yield,
fluoropolymer vessel used, alternative reaction conditions in one step
gave lower yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of 4-tert-Butyl-2,6-dimethylphenylsulfur Trifluoride as a
Deoxofluorinating Agent with High Thermal Stability as Well as Unusual
Resistance to Aqueous Hydrolysis, and Its Diverse Fluorination
Capabilities Including Deoxofluoro-Arylsulfinylation with High
Stereoselectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
