$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 2-L-1,2,4/3,5
1-Acetamido-5-fluoro-2,3,4-tri-O-benzyl-2,3,4-cyclohexanetriol (9). A
mixture of compound 7 (475 mg, 1 mmol) and DAST (0.4 mL, 3 mmol) in
dichloromethane (20 mL) was stirred at 0°C for 4 h and at rt for further
2 h. Then, was added 5 mL of water and this mixture was extracted with
dichloromethane (3 -x 20 mL). The organic layer was submitted to the
usual work-up furnishing a crude residue. Purification by column
chromatography (hexane/ethyl acetate). The compound 9 (70% yield). mp
73-75°C (hexane/ethyl acetate); [α]D 20 - 6 (c 1.3; CH2Cl2). 1H NMR (400
MHz; C 6 D6) δ 0.67 (m, 1H, H-6 a), 0.95 (s, 3H, CH3), 1.85 (m, 1H, H-6
e), 2.62 (dd, 1H, H-2, J2 - 1 = 4.7, J2-3 = 9.0 Hz), 2.77 (m, 1H, H-4),
2.98 (t, 1H, H-3, J3-4 = 8.5 H z ), 3.90 (m, 1H, H -1), 4.08 (m, 1H, H-5,
J5- f = 49, J5 - 4 = 8.5, J5-6e = 3.5, J5- 6a = 9.8 Hz), 3.63-4.26 (m, 6
H, CH2 Ph), 5.20 (d, I Η, NH, Jnh-I= 6.9 Hz), 6.44-6.73 (m, 15H, Ph); 13C
NMR (100.6 MHz, CDCl3) δ 23,3 (CH3), 30.5, 30.7 (C-6 ), 44.2, 44.4 (C
-1), 79.3 (C-2), 80.0, 80.1 (C-3), 82.8, 83.0 (C- 4), 90.3, 92.1
(C-5,J5-F = 177), 170.7 (C = O ). Anal. Calcd for C 2 9 H 3 2 NO 4 F: C,
72.93; H, 6.75; N, 2.93; Found: C, 72.56; H, 6.77; N, 2.78.
