$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (17) General procedure for deoxofluorination.
To a stirred suspension of diethylaminodifluorosulfinium
tetrafluoroborate (4.0 mmol) in dichloromethane (25 mL) at room
temperature was added the substrate (2.67 mmol) and triethylamine
trihydrofluoride (4.0 mmol). The resulting mixture was stirred under
nitrogen over the prescribed amount of time. The reaction was then
quenched at room temperature with a 5% sodium bicarbonate aqueous
solution and stirred for 15 minutes, and the resulting mixture was
extracted twice using dichloromethane. The organic phases were combined,
dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated. The residual
oil was purified by SiO2 chromatography. Fluorooctane. The titled
compound was prepared according to the foregoing procedure using
cyclooctanol (reaction time = 16h). Column chromatography of the crude
material (10% CH2Cl2/pentane) yielded a 77/23 mixture of fluorooctane and
cyclooctene (292mg, 84%) as a clear liquid. 1H NMR (CDCl3) 4.63 (dm, J =
45.9 Hz, 1H), 2.0-1.3 (m, 16H); 19F NMR (CDCl3) -159.65 (s, 1F); 13C NMR
(CDCl3) 94.98 (d, J = 162.9 Hz), 32.30 (d, J = 21.9 Hz), 27.37, 25.31,
22.23 (d, J = 9.7 Hz).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
