$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (E)-1-Fluorooct-2-ene (S5) Under N2 atmosphere, an oven-dried vial was
charged with PhenoFluor (49.9 mg, 0.117 mmol, 1.50 equiv) and KF (9.1 mg,
0.16 mmol, 2.0 equiv). Dichloromethane (1.5 mL) was added, followed by
(E)-oct-2-en-1-ol (10.0 mg, 11.8 μL, 78.0 μM, 1.00 equiv) and
N,N-diisopropylethylamine (27.2 μL, 0.156 mmol, 2.00 equiv). The reaction
mixture was stirred in a sealed vial at 23 °C for 3 h.
3-Nitrofluorobenzene (8.34 μL, 11.0 mg, 78.0 μM, 1.00 equiv) was added as
an internal standard, and the yield was calculated by comparing
integration of the 19F NMR resonance of S5 (-208.7) and S6 (178.8) with
that of 3-nitrofluorobenzene (–112.0 ppm). Yield (19F-NMR): 82% as a 40:1
mixture of S5 : S6. An analytically pure sample of the title compound was
obtained after chromatography on silica gel, eluting with pentane. 82% as
a 40:1 mixture of S5 : S6 Rf = 0.72 (pentane). NMR Spectroscopy: 1H NMR
(400 MHz, C6D6, 23 °C, δ): 5.54–5.46 (m, 2H), 4.50 (dd, J = 49.0, 2.6 Hz,
2H), 1.86–1.78 (m, 2H), 1.38–1.08 (m, 6H), 0.85 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 3H). 13C
NMR (125 MHz, C6D6, 23 °C, δ): 136.8 (d, JCF = 11.0 Hz), 125.2 (d, JCF =
17.4 Hz), 83.2 (d, JCF = 162.9 Hz), 32.4, 31.6, 28.7 (d, JCF = 3.7 Hz),
22.8, 14.2. 19F NMR (375 MHz, C6D6, 23 °C, δ): 208.7.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Schlenk or glovebox technique used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Late-Stage Deoxyfluorination of Alcohols with PhenoFluor
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
